      <memberdef kind="variable" id="namespacetle92466ed_1_1CH__CTRL__REG_1a63042f4a360f3e6e4d1a16fb24e3a310" prot="public" static="no" constexpr="yes" mutable="no">
        <type>constexpr uint8_t</type>
        <definition>constexpr uint8_t tle92466ed::CH_CTRL_REG::MIN_INT_THRESH_FLOOR</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>MIN_INT_THRESH_FLOOR</name>
        <qualifiedname>tle92466ed::CH_CTRL_REG::MIN_INT_THRESH_FLOOR</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= 2u</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Smallest <computeroutput>MIN_INT_THRESH</computeroutput> that keeps the ICC power stage switching. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Datasheet §4.6.2.4: the effective integrator threshold is referenced to the lowest deviation integral captured during the on-phase, so it can go negative. When it does, &quot;the integrated current deviation could not exceed
the zero level and therefore the power stage would not switch on anymore&quot; — the channel stays enabled with its setpoint intact while the load current silently goes to zero. The datasheet&apos;s remedy is to program <computeroutput>MIN_INT_THRESH</computeroutput> greater than 1.</para>
<para>The POR value is 0, so a channel left unconfigured is exposed to this. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="inc/tle92466ed_registers.hpp" line="842" column="19" bodyfile="inc/tle92466ed_registers.hpp" bodystart="842" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="namespacetle92466ed_1_1CH__CTRL__REG_1a8f57caa09252ffa14c6473386963019b" prot="public" static="no" constexpr="yes" mutable="no">
        <type>constexpr uint8_t</type>
        <definition>constexpr uint8_t tle92466ed::CH_CTRL_REG::MIN_INT_THRESH_CEIL</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>MIN_INT_THRESH_CEIL</name>
        <qualifiedname>tle92466ed::CH_CTRL_REG::MIN_INT_THRESH_CEIL</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>= 12u</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Largest <computeroutput>MIN_INT_THRESH</computeroutput> compatible with the Autolimit constraint. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Datasheet §4.6.2.3 requires <computeroutput>AUTO_LIM_VALUE_ABS</computeroutput> &gt; <computeroutput>MIN_INT_THRESH</computeroutput> + 3. With <ref refid="namespacetle92466ed_1_1INTEGRATOR__LIMIT" kindref="compound">INTEGRATOR_LIMIT</ref> left at its POR <computeroutput>AUTO_LIM_VALUE_ABS</computeroutput> of 16 that caps <computeroutput>MIN_INT_THRESH</computeroutput> at 12. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="inc/tle92466ed_registers.hpp" line="852" column="19" bodyfile="inc/tle92466ed_registers.hpp" bodystart="852" bodyend="-1"/>
      </memberdef>
